{"term":"impose","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:fcc2fe3e720bc3e6cc","definition":"To physically lay or place (something) on another thing; to deposit, to put, to set.","example":"[H]is Svvaine / Strevv'd faire greene Oſiers; and impoſ'd thereon / A good ſoft Sheepeskin, vvhich made him a Throne.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee67f93458d54ef0be","definition":"To apply, enforce, or establish (something, often regarded as burdensome as a restriction or tax: see verb sense 1.2.2) with authority.","example":"Congress imposed new tariffs.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bfff19b82dcde38531","definition":"To place or put (something chiefly immaterial, especially something regarded as burdensome as a duty, an encumbrance, a penalty, etc.) on another thing or on someone; to inflict, to repose; also, to place or put (on someone a chiefly immaterial thing, especially something regarded as burdensome).","example":"Social relations impose courtesy.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:17f3c79260b4debb8e","definition":"To force or put (a thing) on someone or something by deceit or stealth; to foist, to obtrude.","example":"I went to visite Mr. Ratcliffe, in whose lodging was an impostor that had like to have impos'd upon us a pretended secret of multiplying gold; 'tis certain he had liv'd some time in Paris in extraordinarie splendor, but I found him to be an egregious cheate.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35ecfca1fc47de320f","definition":"To subject (a student) to imposition (“a task inflicted as punishment”).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, figuratively","register":"UK, figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d7121386233ce768e","definition":"To appoint (someone) to be in authority or command over other people.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, figuratively, obsolete","register":"archaic, figuratively, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:65d7910bbecf2d98ab","definition":"To accuse someone of (a crime, or a sin or other wrongdoing); to charge, to impute.","example":"So, if a Sonne that is by his Father ſent about Merchandize, doe ſinfully miſcarry vpon the Sea; the imputation of his vvickedneſſe, by your rule, ſhould be impoſed vpon his Father that ſent him: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, obsolete","register":"figuratively, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9102706395afc8ae92","definition":"To put (a conclusion or end) to something definitively.","example":"[G]uards vvere held, at all parts, dayes and nights, / For feare of falſe ſurpriſe before, they had impoſde the crovvne / To theſe ſolemnities.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, obsolete","register":"figuratively, obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:178e789411ea632efb","definition":"Chiefly followed by on or upon.","example":"But it is not onely the Difficultie, and Labour, vvhich Men take in finding out of Truth; nor againe, that vvhen it is found, it impoſeth vpon mens Thoughts; that doth bring Lies in fauour: But a naturall, though corrupt Loue, of the Lie it ſelfe.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enjoin","force","inflict","lay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:77308276e78f01b09c","definition":"An act of placing or putting on something chiefly immaterial, especially something regarded as burdensome as a duty, a task, etc.; an imposition.","example":"According to your Ladiſhips impoſe, / I am thus early come, to knovv vvhat ſeruice / It is your pleaſure to command me in.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impose#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪmˈpəʊz/"},"wordFamily":["imposability","imposable","imposal","imposed","imposement","imposer","imposex","imposing","imposing stone","imposing table","imposure","nonimposed","overimpose","preimpose","reimpose","reimposer","self-impose","self-imposed","subimpose","superimpose","superimposed","superimposer","superimposing","superimposure","unimposed"]}